Affected: at 9acff42 (parent of the fix) the shipped runners/tauri.mjs imports
'../../tauri-snapshot.mjs'. The specifier is source-relative (it is correct
only from runners/source/tauri/ before bundling) and the concat bundler copies
it verbatim, so the module graph never resolves: from runners/tauri.mjs it
points two directories above the runner set, and from the extracted native
runner dir (write_embedded_native_runner puts tauri-snapshot.mjs NEXT TO
tauri.mjs) it escapes the managed dir entirely.

Reproduction: node runners/signature_test.mjs at 9acff42 exits 1 with
ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for <two-dirs-up>/tauri-snapshot.mjs imported from
runners/tauri.mjs. The signature-parity CI job on main failed identically
(run 30503009684, job signature-parity). The fix rewrites the authored
specifier to './tauri-snapshot.mjs' (output-relative, like the './web/*.mjs'
oracle imports) and rebundles; the same command exits 0 with 25/25 vectors
passing for both runners.

The same parent commit also broke sdk/reproit_flutter (CI job flutter-sdk,
5 failures): the split moved ReproIt instance plumbing into an
`extension _ReproItRuntime on ReproIt` part file whose unqualified
_maybeEmitInvariants()/_maybeEmitRelations() calls cannot see the class
statics. Qualifying the calls restores compilation; flutter test passes
38/38 after the fix.
